As for the study of the HRP activity, \(10~\upmu\mathrm{L}\) catalysts, containing \(25\mathrm{~\ensuremath~{~\mathrm{~mg\cdotmL^{-1}~}~}~}\) CoBDC-Fc, CoBDC, CoBDC-Fc/HRP, and CoBDC/HRP, 0.28 and \(1.2\ \upmu\mathrm{g}\cdot\mathrm{mL}^{-1}\) HRP were added into the \(100~\upmu\mathrm{L}\) HAc-NaAc buffer \((\mathrm{pH}\,4.0)\) and \(100\ \mathrm{mM}\ \mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}\) \((100~\upmu\mathrm{L})\) mixture solution, respectively. Then, \(1~\mathrm{mM}\) TMB \((100~\upmu\mathrm{L})\) was introduced into the above solution and monitored the variations of absorbance values with reaction time, immediately.
As for the study of the GOx activity, different catalysts \((50~\upmu\mathrm{L})\) , containing \(1\ \mathrm{mg\cdotmL^{-1}}\) CoBDC-Fc, CoBDC, CoBDC-Fc/GOx, and CoBDC/GOx, 11 and \(18\ \upmu\mathrm{g}\cdot\mathrm{mL}^{-1}\) GOx were added into the \(500\,\upmu\mathrm{L}\) HAc-NaAc buffer \((\mathrm{pH}\,6.0)\) and \(1~\mathrm{~mL~}\) glucose \((1\,\mathrm{\mM})\) and incubation for \(0.5\,\mathrm{~h~}\) at \(57\ ^{\circ}\mathrm{C}.\) . Then, the reaction solution was centrifuged to remove the CoBDC-Fc, CoBDC, CoBDC-Fc/GOx, and CoBDC/GOx for circumvention of the influence of nanomaterials. The obtained supernatant \((100~\upmu\mathrm{L})\) was added to the \(10~\upmu\mathrm{L}\) HRP \((1~\upmu\mathrm{g}\cdot\mathrm{mL}^{-1})\) , \(100~\upmu\mathrm{L}\) HAc-NaAc buffer \((\mathrm{pH}\,4.0)\) , and \(1~\mathrm{mM}\) TMB \((100~\upmu\mathrm{L})\) mixture solution. After incubation for \(5\,\mathrm{min}\) , the absorption spectra were recorded for further assay.
